# Which ramp is fastest?
subtitle: "A straight ramp, a steep drop, or a swooping curve: tap the one that wins the race, then hear how Newton solved it overnight."
voices: {"a":"gemini:Laomedeia | an upbeat, playful quiz host; light and quick","take":"lines"}

## Which ramp is fastest?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: brach
      title: Brachistochrone curve
      authors: Wikipedia; V. F. Rickey, 'History of the brachistochrone'
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brachistochrone_curve
      finding: Johann Bernoulli posed the problem in June 1696; Newton received it on 29 January 1697 and, by his niece Catherine Conduitt's account, had solved it by 4 am; Bernoulli recognised the anonymous solution 'tanquam ex ungue leonem'

